# Files excluded from `@expo/fingerprint` hashing.
#
# NOTE: runtimeVersion uses the "appVersion" policy, so the fingerprint no
# longer determines the runtime version and can no longer fail a build. This
# file exists so that `eas fingerprint:compare --build-id <ID>` stays useful as
# the manual "did native code actually change?" check before publishing an OTA
# update. Without these rules that comparison is drowned in tooling noise.
#
# CocoaPods rewrites both of these on every `pod install` -- project.pbxproj
# gets freshly generated random UUIDs for each Pods file reference, and
# Podfile.lock records the CocoaPods version that produced it. Neither reflects
# a real change to the app.
ios/Podfile.lock
ios/**/project.pbxproj

# A local Android build (expo run:android) makes Gradle rewrite this library
# manifest in place, stripping package="org.reactnative.maskedview" as part of
# the AGP 8 namespace migration. EAS installs pristine via `npm ci`, so the two
# disagree until node_modules is reinstalled.
node_modules/@react-native-masked-view/masked-view/android/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
